      "text": "Great question for a structural analysis! Let me try to get the actual chapter-by-chapter text to map this out accurately for you.",
      "mediaUrl": null
    },
    {
      "text": "The search snippets aren't granular enough. Let me try to retrieve the actual book text to map the chapter structure accurately.",
      "mediaUrl": null
    },
    {
      "text": "I was able to retrieve a small opening passage, but I don't have enough granular chapter-level data to give you a reliable, accurate chapter-by-chapter breakdown of the alternating structure. I want to be straightforward with you about that rather than risk giving you inaccurate structural details you'd use in a published review.\n\nHere is what I **can confirm with confidence** from the sources retrieved:\n\n---\n\n### What Is Verified About the Structure\n\n- The novel uses a **dual timeline** that alternates between a **present-day thread** (Poppy and Alex's reunion trip) and a series of **past summer flashbacks** that recount each of their annual vacations over roughly a decade.\n- The opening passage (retrieved directly from the text) establishes Poppy as the narrator and frames the central tension immediately: *\"That was nine summers ago. This year, for the first time, we were not going to—\"* — signaling that the present and past are in direct conversation from page one.\n- The flashback chapters are not all from the same year — they move through **multiple summers**, progressively building toward the pivotal falling-out rather than focusing on just one past moment. This is what distinguishes Henry's structure from a simpler \"then vs. now\" setup.\n- The alternating structure creates **dramatic irony**: readers gradually piece together what went wrong between Poppy and Alex before it's explicitly stated, while simultaneously watching them navigate the fragile reunion in the present.\n\n---\n\n### What I'd Caution Against Stating Without Verification\n\nI wouldn't want you to assert in your review a specific chapter count, the exact labeling of each chapter (e.g., whether they're titled by year or by trip destination), or a precise alternating pattern (e.g., \"every other chapter\") without verifying that against the physical book. Those granular details vary by edition and are easy to misremember or misreport.\n\n---\n\n### My Recommendation\n\nFor the structural analysis in your review, the safest and most analytically rich approach is to discuss **the effect of the structure** rather than cataloguing it mechanically — which is also more compelling for readers. If you do have access to a copy of the book, I'd encourage you to flip through and note the chapter headings yourself for any specific citations. Would you like help framing the structural analysis in your review language instead?",
      "mediaUrl": null
    }
  ],
